# Reuse components

Before adding markup, look in `src/components` for a component that already does the job. Import its barrel (`@/components/ui/Atoms/Button`, `@/components/ui/Breadcrumbs`). Do not copy a second button, banner, empty state, breadcrumb, dialog, or page header.

- Buttons are `Button`, `ButtonLink`, or `ButtonAnchor` from `@/components/ui/Atoms/Button`.
- Radio choices are `RadioGroup` from `@/components/ui/RadioGroup`. Do not hand-write a second set of radio inputs.
- Trails are `Breadcrumbs` from `@/components/ui/Breadcrumbs`.
- Page chrome is `LandingHeader` or `ProjectPageHeader` from `@/components/library`.
- Empty, status, and help copy use `EmptyState`, `Banner`, and `HelpPopover` when those already fit.

If a second screen needs the same piece, extend the existing component or extract one shared component. Do not leave a near-copy in the page.

```tsx
// The page title lives in the shared header. Nested pages add crumbs.
<ProjectPageHeader
  projectId={projectId}
  title="Maps"
  crumbs={[{ href: worldHref, label: "World" }, { label: "Maps", current: true }]}
/>
```
